Z||000000||Robert||07-22-2001||08:43 PM||||I’ve got my 87GT sitting out in the sun lately, and the steering wheel is leaking chocolate by the end of the day.  I’ve heard the fix is to use some type of glue to seal the stitching.  Anyone had success with this treatment; and if so, what kind of glue did you use?<BR>Thanks in advance.<BR>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."<P>Will Rogers, U.S. Writer and Humorist||||reg||5
Z||000001||Mach10||07-22-2001||09:03 PM||||I don't recommend using Nestle Quik again...<BR>Maybe contact cement? I use that on anything fabric-like, but I don't know what kind of heat tolerance it has. Why don't you buy a small tube, and bond two chunks of vinyl together, put it on the dash, and test it when things heat up?||||reg||7
Z||000002||fiero56||07-22-2001||09:05 PM||||I'm going to attemt replacing the leather with a combo from here: <A HREF="http://www.wheelskins.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.wheelskins.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||hobbitt||07-23-2001||09:01 PM||||my 84 did that turned out it was a sublayer cushion they put in from factory to give that cushion feel. everytime it got hoyt after it started to do it the wheel turned to mush in my fingertips, hot mush at that. I had to get a new steering wheel.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Toddster||07-23-2001||10:14 PM||||Hobbitt is right. The foam padding of your steering wheel like your headliner and sunvisors will deteriorate over time. That is why the leather on your steering wheel gets mushy. The best solution is to have the wheel re-upholstered. I know a guy who will do it for $150. Just send him the wheel and a check. Takes a week or so. That's the best price I've seen and he is a Fiero fan.<P>email me if you want his number||||reg||1
Z||000005||jelly2m8||07-23-2001||10:15 PM||||heh, we had a joke fer this natural phenomenom, we call it the "gummy" wheel...;p||||reg||1
Z||000006||Robert||07-23-2001||11:04 PM||||My wheel is not mushy at all.  I’m just trying to keep it that way.  I only loose a drop or two per hot day, but in time I’m sure it will get mushy.  I’m going to try some white glue on one section this week and see how it holds up over the weekend while it’s at the used car lot. <BR>BTW   you can check out car ad here if you are interested. <A HREF="http://www.autofairs.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.autofairs.com/</A> <BR>Just do a search under “Pontiac”/”Fiero” <BR>Thanks<BR>Robert<BR>||||reg||1
