Z||000008||Robert||07-29-2001||11:00 PM||||Well after this weekend I can tell you what doesn’t work.<BR>Elmer’s Glue-All white glue.<BR>Next weekend I’ll try something else .....<BR>Any ideas?<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000009||Formula88||07-29-2001||11:09 PM||||Go to a craft store (Michael's, A.C. Moore, etc) and get a glue made for leather or fabric.  That should work fine.||||reg||6
Z||000010||mrfixit58||07-30-2001||03:22 PM||||If any of the goo has dripped on your fabric seats, use WD-40 and a clean cotton rag to get it out. I had a puddle of that goo on an otherwise perfect seat cover. After several soakings/scrubbings with the WD-40, I used a little upholstery cleaner and a wet-vac and the spot can totally out.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||3
